== verdict
==============================================================================
  !! AVAS chose different active spaces along the scan: [(np.int64(10), 6), (np.int64(12), 7)]. Energies at points with a different space
     are not on the same footing; treat the curves as suspect.
  smallest root 1 - root 0 gap: 0.078 eV at r = 3.20 A  (grid spacing 0.100 A)
  dipoles: root 0 |mu| 4.40 -> 5.00 D, root 1 4.28 -> 4.90 D across r = 3.00-3.20 A  -> not exchanged
  dominant-configuration weight dip near the minimum: root 0 0.01, root 1 -0.02 below their scan medians  -> no localised mixing
  05 UCCSD(T) max T1 at r = 2.60 A, 0.60 A from the gap minimum

  -> INCONCLUSIVE at this resolution. Rerun on a narrow window around 3.20 A,
     e.g. --rmin 3.00 --rmax 3.40 --npoints 17.

  Landau-Zener estimate of staying DIABATIC: P = 0.22
     (H12 38.9 meV, dF 0.0045 Ha/bohr, E_kin 1.02 eV, v 1.89e-03 au)
     Rough, 1D and classical. The sampled gap can only be LARGER than the
     true minimum on this grid, so the true P is at least this large.
     Neither limit holds: this region needs the two states propagated
     together with their coupling.

  cost: 9981 CPU-s over 16 points (624 CPU-s/point, 5.2 min wall)
